Subject: [PATCH] A light stops at the first thing it meets, as a row of candidates

Patch 0049 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-08, in the Fire Temple, of the carved faces with a flame in each mouth: "the
fires here ... cause some sort of polygonal cutouts from mainly front angles", and then the rule:
"it should be just like link where point lights like torches or navi, hit an object but then never
past it. pretty much all solid geometry like walls statues, enemies, trees etc, if the light hits
hit the light must not pass through and instead cast shadows".

The last 48 units before every light that was not white went untraced (LightClearance, so a sconce
would not shadow its own flame). These flames' lights sit five to ten units from the stone of the
mouth, so inside that ball the statue did not exist for them: their light went through it. 286
flames are placed by the rooms; none sits inside stone and about eighty sit in a niche like these.

A local light's shadow ray (the surface pass and the dust) now runs to the flame's own size for
every light and skips a surface it meets from its outside, which faces away from the light
(RAY_FLAG_CULL_FRONT_FACING_TRIANGLES: the game draws the outside, the cross of a triangle's first
two edges, which DXR names the front). Anything between the surface and the light is left through a
side facing the light and stops it; a niche lets its flame out of the opening only; a light inside a
closed body (a Poe's lantern) is not swallowed by it; a draw shown from both sides blocks from both,
the flag not applying to it. The glow in the air takes one such ray per light per pixel, from the
point of the pixel's ray nearest the light.

The user asked for candidates to cycle rather than one answer ("adds some debugging options to cycle
through so I can test a bunch of different options to see which one fixes it without regressions"),
so the Debugging menu's Light through stone row chooses, in tuneLightTest.x (a new parameter group):
0 all of it, 1 the same with the glow in the air unshadowed, 2 the 48 unit clearance as in 0.4.0.
Beams and windows (0029 to 0045) are untouched.

diff --git a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
--- a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
+++ b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
@@ -530,11 +530,86 @@ float lightFalloff(float distance2, float radius2, float core2) {
     const float window = saturate(1.0f - ratio * ratio);
     return inverse * window * window;
 }
-static const float LightClearance = 48.0f;   // world units around a light its holder may fill (a sconce's bracket)
+static const float LightClearance = 48.0f;   // world units around a light its holder may fill (a sconce's bracket); since patch 0049 only the Light through stone row's 0.4.0 candidate
 // A local light's shadow ray starts this far along itself, so a floor cannot shadow itself at a
 // grazing angle to a torch a few steps away (2026-09-24, the bands across the Deku Tree floor).
 static const float LocalBlockerSkip = 10.0f;   // world units; Link is about 60
 
+// A LIGHT STOPS AT THE FIRST THING IT MEETS (patch 0049, the user, 2026-10-08, of the Fire Temple's
+// carved faces with a flame in each mouth: "the fires here ... cause some sort of polygonal cutouts",
+// and then the cause in their own words, "since its a sphere could it be because its nested in the
+// statues mouth and the spheres being cropped by geomety but the light is still travelling through
+// it and out the other side rather than stopping? ... pretty much all solid geometry like walls
+// statues, enemies, trees etc, if the light hits hit the light must not pass through and instead
+// cast shadows").
+//
+// They were right. The last 48 units before every light that was not white went untraced
+// (LightClearance), so a flame would not be shadowed by its own sconce. These flames (EnLight, its
+// light forty units up the flame) sit five to ten units from the stone of the mouth they burn in,
+// so inside that ball the statue did not exist for their light: it went through the stone and lit
+// what stood behind and beside the statue, while stone further out did stop it, and the line
+// between the two was the polygon. An inventory of every flame the rooms place (286, 2026-10-08)
+// found none inside stone and about eighty in a niche like these, all leaking the same way.
+//
+// What the clearance was for is kept a different way, by which SIDE of a surface the ray meets.
+// The game draws the outside of a thing (its triangles' outward side is the cross of their first
+// two edges, in the order the renderer keeps), and DXR names that side the front. A shadow ray runs
+// from the lit surface toward the light, so:
+//   - a wall, a statue, an enemy or a figure between the two is entered through its near side
+//     (front, skipped) and left through its far side, which faces the light and is met from
+//     behind (kept): it stops the light and casts its shadow;
+//   - a flame in a niche: the niche's walls face the light, and every ray from outside reaches
+//     one from behind, unless it comes through the opening: the light leaves by the mouth alone;
+//   - a light carried INSIDE a closed thing (a Poe's lantern, a glow in a body) meets only that
+//     thing's outer skin, from outside (front, skipped), so its own holder never swallows it;
+//   - a draw the game shows from both sides (leaves, cloth, a fence: culling off) has culling off
+//     in the traced scene too, the ray flag does not apply to it, and it blocks from either side.
+// So the only clearance left is the flame's own size, which every light gets, as Navi already did.
+//
+// AS CANDIDATES ON A ROW (the user, 2026-10-08: "adds some debugging options to cycle through so I
+// can test a bunch of different options to see which one fixes it without regressions"; and "my
+// current 4.0 is really good so i neevr want to accidentally regress"). The Debugging menu's Light
+// through stone row, tuneLightTest.x: 0 all of the above; 1 the same with the glow in the air left
+// unshadowed (glowThroughStone); 2 the 48 unit clearance and the untested sides, as in 0.4.0.
+bool lightsThroughStone() {
+    return RtParams.tuneLightTest.x == 2.0f;
+}
+
+bool glowThroughStone() {
+    return RtParams.tuneLightTest.x != 0.0f;
+}
+
+// How much of the ray's end, at the light, goes untraced.
+float lightClearance(PointLight light) {
+    if (lightsThroughStone() && ((light.groupBits & 4u) == 0u)) {
+        return max(light.pointRadius, LightClearance);
+    }
+
+    return light.pointRadius;
+}
+
+// A local light's shadow ray: traceVisibilityRange, but a surface met from its outside, which faces
+// away from the light, does not stop it.
+float traceLightVisibility(float3 origin, float3 direction, float tMin, float tMax, out float hitDistance) {
+    if (lightsThroughStone()) {
+        return traceVisibilityRange(origin, direction, tMin, tMax, hitDistance);
+    }
+
+    RayDesc ray;
+    ray.Origin = origin;
+    ray.Direction = direction;
+    ray.TMin = tMin;
+    ray.TMax = tMax;
+
+    ShadowPayload payload;
+    payload.visibility = 1.0f;
+    payload.hitDistance = 0.0f;
+    TraceRay(SceneBVH, RAY_FLAG_ACCEPT_FIRST_HIT_AND_END_SEARCH | RAY_FLAG_SKIP_CLOSEST_HIT_SHADER | RAY_FLAG_CULL_FRONT_FACING_TRIANGLES,
+             DepthRayQueryMask, 1, 0, 1, ray, payload);
+    hitDistance = payload.hitDistance;
+    return payload.visibility;
+}
+
 // A BEAM (patch 0029): a shaft of light the game draws, found by its shape on the CPU
 // (rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp, beamFromDraw) and handed over in the light list with this group
 // bit. It is not a point: it is a cylinder of light falling down its own axis, so it lights what
@@ -809,10 +884,12 @@ void LightsRayGen() {
         // through him (the user, 2026-09-24: "she only causes proper shadow when out to the side
         // but directly on top it disapears"; "the light should never pass through an object to
         // reach it"). She gets her own point radius instead, and every other light keeps the 48.
+        //
+        // SINCE PATCH 0049 EVERY LIGHT IS TRACED TO ITS FLAME (lightClearance): the 48 units let a
+        // flame in a niche shine through the stone around it, and its holder is now left out by
+        // the side of it the ray meets (traceLightVisibility) instead.
         float hitDistance;
-        const float clearance = ((light.groupBits & 4u) != 0u)
-            ? light.pointRadius
-            : max(light.pointRadius, LightClearance);
+        const float clearance = lightClearance(light);
         // The disc sampled properly: one point per sample, each from its own blue noise, and
         // the index carries the light as well as the sample so two lights never take the same
         // point on their own discs.
@@ -826,7 +903,7 @@ void LightsRayGen() {
             const float targetDistance = length(toTarget);
             const float tMax = max(targetDistance - clearance, 0.0f);
             const float sample = (tMax > LocalBlockerSkip)
-                ? traceVisibilityRange(shadowOrigin, toTarget / targetDistance, LocalBlockerSkip, tMax, hitDistance)
+                ? traceLightVisibility(shadowOrigin, toTarget / targetDistance, LocalBlockerSkip, tMax, hitDistance)
                 : 1.0f;
             blocked += 1.0f - sample;
         }
@@ -1553,10 +1630,9 @@ float3 dustLightAt(float3 p, uint2 launchIndex) {
         }
 
         const float distance = sqrt(distance2);
-        const float clearance = ((light.groupBits & 4u) != 0u) ? light.pointRadius : max(light.pointRadius, LightClearance);
-        const float tMax = max(distance - clearance, 0.0f);
+        const float tMax = max(distance - lightClearance(light), 0.0f);   // patch 0049
         float hitDistance;
-        const float visibility = (tMax > 1.0f) ? traceVisibilityRange(p, toLight / distance, 0.0f, tMax, hitDistance) : 1.0f;
+        const float visibility = (tMax > 1.0f) ? traceLightVisibility(p, toLight / distance, 0.0f, tMax, hitDistance) : 1.0f;
         const float core2 = light.attenuationExponent * light.attenuationExponent;
         local += light.diffuseColor * (lightFalloff(distance2, radius2, core2) * visibility);
     }
@@ -1817,6 +1893,38 @@ void ScatterRayGen() {
     const uint lights = min(RtParams.lightsCount, RtParams.maxLights);
     const float3 noise = getBlueNoise(gBlueNoise, launchIndex, FrParams.frameCount + 41);
     const float step = end / float(ScatterSteps);
+    // THE GLOW STOPS AT STONE TOO (patch 0049, the user's rule above traceLightVisibility). A
+    // light's glow was a ball of lit air with nothing in its way, so a flame in a statue's mouth
+    // hung its glow round the statue's sides and back, where its light cannot reach. One ray per
+    // light per pixel decides it, from the point of this pixel's ray nearest the light (where its
+    // glow is brightest) to the light: a ray for every step would put the shadow's edge in the air
+    // at a different place each frame, and the glow keeps no history to settle it. Lights past
+    // the thirty second are left as they were. The Light through stone row's first candidate only.
+    uint glowBlocked = 0u;
+    if ((lightGlow > 0.0f) && (RtParams.tuneExperiment.x != 4.0f) && !glowThroughStone()) {
+        const float glowScale = max(RtParams.tuneBounce.z, 0.01f);
+        for (uint i = 0; i < min(lights, 32u); i++) {
+            const PointLight light = SceneLights[i];
+            if ((light.groupBits & (BeamLightBit | WindowLightBit | AirMoverBit)) != 0u) {
+                continue;
+            }
+
+            const float tNearest = clamp(dot(light.position - origin, direction), 0.0f, end);
+            const float3 nearest = origin + direction * tNearest;
+            const float3 toLight = light.position - nearest;
+            const float distance = length(toLight);
+            const float tMax = distance - lightClearance(light);
+            if ((distance >= light.attenuationRadius * glowScale) || (tMax <= 1.0f)) {
+                continue;
+            }
+
+            float hitDistance;
+            if (traceLightVisibility(nearest, toLight / distance, 1.0f, tMax, hitDistance) < 0.5f) {
+                glowBlocked |= 1u << i;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     float3 sum = 0.0f;
     for (uint s = 0; s < ScatterSteps; s++) {
         const float t = (float(s) + noise.x) * step;
@@ -1839,6 +1947,10 @@ void ScatterRayGen() {
                     continue;
                 }
 
+                if ((i < 32u) && (((glowBlocked >> i) & 1u) != 0u)) {   // stone between it and this pixel's air (patch 0049)
+                    continue;
+                }
+
                 const float3 toLight = light.position - p;
                 const float distance2 = dot(toLight, toLight);
                 // THE GLOW'S OWN SIZE (2026-09-24, the user: "control the reach and the actual
